course: dictionary
lesson: 2638
title: Destructive: words that show damage
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «The destructive storm tore the roofs off houses and snapped the trees.» You do not need a dictionary for this one. Storms snap trees and tear off roofs, so destructive must mean causing damage. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "The damaging storm tore the roofs off houses" still makes sense.
explain: Destructive is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a destructive storm, a destructive puppy, a destructive villain. Its comparison words are more destructive and most destructive, as in «the most destructive bombs ever made».
explain: The word can describe animals and people too. «A bored pet can become unhappy and destructive.» The pet is not wicked. It is bored and breaking things, and the sentence tells you what helps: toys, play, walks and new things to sniff.
fact: Destructive means causing a lot of damage or ruin.
fact: «Destructive» is an adjective, so it describes a thing, an animal or a person.
fact: The comparisons are «more destructive» and «most destructive».
fact: «Destructive» comes from the verb «destroy», so the two words are related.
fact: Bored animals can become destructive, so they need toys, play, walks and new things to sniff.
exercise: «The destructive storm tore the roofs off houses.» What does destructive mean here? | Gentle and calm | Very cold and icy | *Causing a lot of damage | Bright and sunny
exercise: A bored puppy chews shoes and rips up cushions. Which word describes the puppy? | Sleepy | *Destructive | Calm | Tidy
exercise: «The villain wrecked the town, the most destructive in the whole story.» Which word is the top form of destructive? | destructive | *most | more | town
test: «Destructive» is closest in meaning to which word? | Helpful | Quiet | *Damaging | Beautiful
test: «Earthquakes and fires can be destructive.» In this sentence, what can earthquakes and fires do? | *Cause a lot of damage | Keep people warm | Make music | Help farmers grow crops
exam: «A bored pet can become unhappy and destructive; toys, play, walks and new things to sniff keep it happy.» What keeps a bored pet from becoming destructive? | Shouting at it | Being left alone all day | *Toys, play, walks and new things to sniff | Locking it in the garden
